   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/1ppp1ppp/p1n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N2NP1/PPPP1P1P/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "a6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black's a6 is a nothing move here. Don't fear ...b5, and resist the instinct to play a4 — that would only weaken the b4 square and do more harm than good.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "don’t weaken b4 answering a harmless ...a6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 1298,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/1ppp1ppp/p1n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N2NP1/PPPP1PBP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Bg2"
   ],
   "spoken": "We just keep developing with the bishop to g2, the Glek's fianchetto.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 1304,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/1ppp1ppp/p1n2n2/4p3/1b2P3/2N2NP1/PPPP1PBP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [
    "Bb4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 1327.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/1ppp1ppp/p1n2n2/4p3/1b2P3/2N2NP1/PPPP1PBP/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 3 6",
   "line": [
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "When Black pins with the bishop to b4, don't reflexively play d3 — Black isn't actually winning a pawn. We simply castle.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "don’t defend a pawn that isn’t really hanging"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 1329,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/1ppp1ppp/p1n2n2/4p3/4P3/2b2NP1/PPPP1PBP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 7",
